  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Food Safety Officer vs Joseph John on 17 September, 2025",
    "facts": "2. The allegation is that on 23.03.2015, the Food Safety Officer inspected Archana Bakery, Marangattupally, and purchased banana chips, and the samples were sent for chemical analysis. It was tested as per standard food safety 2025:KER:69312 CRL.REV.PET NO. 338 OF 2023 parameters and found non-conforming as it shows the presence of Synthetic colour Tartrazine, which is in contravention of the rules. 3.Thereafter, the respondents filed an application for discharge before the learned Magistrate as C.M.P No. 4101(A)/2019. 4.The learned Magistrate, as per the impugned order, invoked Section 258 Cr. P.C. and accordingly dropped the proceedings against the accused. Aggrieved by the same, this revision petition is filed by the Food Safety Officer. 5. Admittedly, the petitioner filed a private complaint before the Judicial First Class Magistrate Court-I, Pala, alleging offences under the Food Safety and Standards (Food Product Standards and Food Additives) regulations 2011.",
    "arguments": "\"258. Power to stop proceedings in certain cases. In any summons-case instituted otherwise than upon complaint, a Magistrate of the first class or, with the previous sanction of the Chief Judicial Magistrate, any other Judicial Magistrate, may, for reasons to be recorded by him, stop the proceedings at any stage without pronouncing any judgment and where such stoppage of proceedings is made after the evidence of the principal witnesses has been recorded, pronounce a judgment of acquittal, and in any other case, release the accused, and such release shall have the effect of discharge.\"",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "\"258. Power to stop proceedings in certain cases. In any summons-case instituted otherwise than upon complaint, a Magistrate of the first class or, with the previous sanction of the Chief Judicial Magistrate, any other Judicial Magistrate, may, for reasons to be recorded by him, stop the proceedings at any stage without pronouncing any judgment and where such stoppage of proceedings is made after the evidence of the principal witnesses has been recorded, pronounce a judgment of acquittal, and in any other case, release the accused, and such release shall have the effect of discharge.\""
  },
